<title>FRANCE: No question of changing franc/mark parity - Arthuis.</title>
<headline>No question of changing franc/mark parity - Arthuis.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said there was no question of changing the parity between the franc and the mark.</p>
<p>&quot;(We will) certainly not change the parity between the franc and the mark,&quot; Arthuis said during parliamentary questions when asked about businesses and the impact of the franc's parity.</p>
<p>He also said the fixing of foreign exchange parities ahead of the start of a single currency would be based on the pivot rates in the European Exchange Rate Mechanism.  </p>
<p>&quot;This will be done necessarily on the basis of the established stabilities, on the basis of the pivot rates which will have been essentially accepted by the markets.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
